# slug: ch20-points-to
# source: chapters/ch20.tex:76 (approximate line of \begin{algorithm})
# caption: Worklist solver for inclusion points-to constraints
# label: alg:ch20-points-to
# require: finite closed-world constraints over pointer cells and abstract objects
# ensure: least fixed point of all points-to sets
# keywords: INPUT/OUTPUT/REQUIRE/ENSURE/FOR/FORALL/WHILE/IF/ELSE/RETURN

REQUIRE finite closed-world constraints over pointer cells and abstract objects
ENSURE least fixed point of all points-to sets
set every pts(v) to {}
place every constraint on the worklist W
WHILE W != {} DO
  remove a constraint c from W
  evaluate c using current sets, registering every set read as a dependency
  union its contributions into the destination sets
  IF some target set gained a new object THEN
    add every constraint reading that set to W
  END IF
END WHILE

